From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:17:34 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 30/97] Plutonium: embedded focus follows modal dialogs
 (xdg_dialog_v1)

EXO-MODAL: Exo implements xdg_wm_dialog_v1 (GTK 4, Qt 6), so it knows a
toplevel is modal to its parent (ShellSurfaceBase::modal_to_parent()).
While a page shows the dialog, embedded focus on the parent goes to it:
EmbeddedWindows::Focus() of the parent focuses the dialog, and a dialog
mapped, made modal or attached over the focused window takes its focus,
so the page reports the dialog focused rather than the parent (whose
client sends its keys to the dialog anyway). When the focused dialog
closes or leaves the page, focus goes back to its parent.
